    "https://www.hu-berlin.de/en/university/working-at-the-hu/jobs/details/wissenschaftlicher-mitarbeiterin-m-w-d-in-der-emmy-noether-forschungsgruppe-theoretical-transport-physics-t2p-dr-175-26": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (m/f/d) in the Emmy Noether research group Theoretical Transport Physics (T2P)",
      "description": "Research Fellow (m/f/d) in the Emmy Noether research group Theoretical Transport Physics (T2P) expected 75 % part-time employment - E 13 TV-L HU (third-party funding limited for 9 month) At a glance Job category Academic staff Organization Faculty of Mathematics and Natural Sciences Department of Physics Location Zum Großen Windkanal 2, 12489 Berlin Reference number DR/175/26 Time limitation in months 9 Pay grade E13 Job scope Teilzeit (29.55 Hours weekly) Number of vacancies 1 Application deadline 11. Nov 2026 Apply now Founded in 1810, Humboldt-Universität zu Berlin is one of Germany's leading universities. As a comprehensive university with over 36,000 students, it combines research excellence with innovative support for young talents. Their international networks, interdisciplinary research collaborations, and progressive teaching concepts shape Berlin as a center of science. The Humboldt-Universität zu Berlin holds the status of a university of excellence. Your responsibilities scientific service in research in the Emmy Noether research group Theoretical Transport Physics (T2P) timely attendance of regular meetings with the group carrying out analytical calculations implementing scientific software within the elphbolt code base carrying out numerical computations supporting collaborative work preparing manuscripts for publication presenting results at international conferences organizing internal events such as workshops and colloquiums What you bring to the table completed scientific university education (Master’s degree) in physics with a strong specialization in theoretical many-body physics evidenced by a Master’s thesis on the topic or a publication on the topic demonstrable experience in analytical calculations in the field of many-body physics demonstrable experience in developing parallel scientific software using modern Fortran within at least one open-source code base full professional proficiency (C1) in English Your path to the HU Please send your complete application, referencing the job ID DR/175/26 to Humboldt-Universität zu Berlin, Faculty of Mathematics and Natural Sciences, Department of Physics, Dr. Nakib Protik (located: Zum Großen Windkanal 2, 12489 Berlin), Unter den Linden 6, 10099 Berlin or preferably in electronic form as a single PDF file to nakib.protik ☞ Please insert an @ at this point ☜ physik.hu-berlin ☞ Please insert a period at this point de , entering <Your last name>_MT_2027_T2P in the subject line. Since we will not return your documents, please submit copies in the application only. The application will be a single PDF file with just the following (and nothing else): Required application documents: letter of motivation (stating the motivation to join the T2P group, highlighting the fit to the stated requirements, and prior research experience) tabular curriculum vitae, including links to the Master’s thesis or published papers copies of certificates contact details of at least two reference letter writers (do not include the reference letters) Applications prepared in a different format will not be accepted. If you have further questions about the job posting or the scope of duties, please do not hesitate to contact Dr. Nakib H. Protik ( nakib.protik ☞ Please insert an @ at this point ☜ physik.hu-berlin ☞ Please insert a period at this point de ). The position is scheduled to be filled on the earliest possible date. The Humboldt-Universität zu Berlin is seeking to increase the proportion of women in research and teaching, and specifically encourages qualified female scholars to apply. Severely disabled applicants with equivalent qualifications will be given preferential consideration. People with an immigration history are specifically encouraged to apply. Since we will not return your documents, please submit copies in the application only. The Humboldt-Universität zu Berlin is bound by collective agreements and applies the TV-L HU. Information on pay grading and the annual salary scale can be found here: https://hu.berlin/ETRL . Information pursuant to Art. 12, 13 DSGVO on the processing of personal data at Humboldt-Universität zu Berlin within the framework of job advertisements can be found on our website: https://hu.berlin/DSGVO . Please visit our website which gives you access to the legally binding German version. Submit application Contact person Dr. Nakib Protik Nachwuchsgruppenleiter Tel.: +49 30 2093-82570 Email: nakib.protik ☞ Please insert an @ at this point ☜ hu-berlin ☞ Please insert a period at this point de to profile page of Dr. Nakib Protik Department of Physics Address Lise-Meitner-Haus, Newtonstraße 15, 12489 Berlin General contact Tel.: +49 30 2093-82000 idir.physik ☞ Please insert an @ at this point ☜ hu-berlin ☞ Please insert a period at this point de"
    },
    "https://www.hu-berlin.de/en/university/working-at-the-hu/jobs/details/wissenschaftlicher-mitarbeiterin-m-w-d-im-bereich-technische-informatik-an-229-26": {
      "title": "Research Associate (m/f/d) in the field of Computer Engineering",
      "description": "Research Associate (m/f/d) in the field of Computer Engineering limited to 4 years - E 13 TV-L HU At a glance Job category Academic staff Organization Faculty of Mathematics and Natural Sciences Department of Computer Science Location Johann-von-Neumann-Haus, Rudower Chaussee 25, 12489 Berlin Reference number AN/229/26 Time limitation in months 48 Pay grade E13 Job scope Vollzeit (39.4 Hours weekly) Number of vacancies 1 Application deadline 11. Nov 2026 Apply now Founded in 1810, Humboldt-Universität zu Berlin is one of Germany's leading universities. As a comprehensive university with over 36,000 students, it combines research excellence with innovative support for young talents. Their international networks, interdisciplinary research collaborations, and progressive teaching concepts shape Berlin as a center of science. The Humboldt-Universität zu Berlin holds the status of a university of excellence. Your responsibilities research work in the field of Computer Engineering on the topic of reconfigurable processor architectures development, implementation and evaluation of novel hardware, including AI-assisted hardware, as well as the software for its programming and operation publication and presentation of research results at scientific conferences and in academic journals teaching duties amounting to 4 teaching hours per week (LVS) assisting with organisational tasks of the chair and with research grant applications tasks for personal scientific qualification (doctorate/PhD) What you bring to the table What we expect from you completed university degree (Master’s or equivalent) in engineering or a comparable field with a technical focus, or a computer science background excellent command of German, both written and spoken (at least C1-level) What would be desirable academic teaching experience in university courses What we offer a modern work environment a pay scale classification (TV-L) high responsibility in different working fields structured orientation and onboarding flexible working hours (flexitime) excellent opportunities for further training As a family-friendly university, we promote the compatibility of work and family life. Your path to the HU Please send your complete application, referencing the job ID AN/229/26 to Humboldt-Universität zu Berlin, Faculty of Mathematics and Natural Sciences, Department of Computer Science , Prof. Michael Hübner (located: Rudower Chaussee 25, 12489 Berlin), Unter den Linden 6, 10099 Berlin or preferably in electronic form as a single PDF file to michael.huebner ☞ Please insert an @ at this point ☜ hu-berlin ☞ Please insert a period at this point de . Required application documents: letter of motivation tabular curriculum vitae proof of the required qualification (certificates, diplomas, continuing education certificates) work references or evaluations If you have further questions about the job posting or the scope of duties, please do not hesitate to contact Prof. Michael Hübner ( michael.huebner ☞ Please insert an @ at this point ☜ hu-berlin ☞ Please insert a period at this point de ). The position is scheduled to be filled on January 1, 2027. The Humboldt-Universität zu Berlin is seeking to increase the proportion of women in research and teaching, and specifically encourages qualified female scholars to apply. Severely disabled applicants with equivalent qualifications will be given preferential consideration. People with an immigration history are specifically encouraged to apply. Since we will not return your documents, please submit copies in the application only. The Humboldt-Universität zu Berlin is bound by collective agreements and applies the TV-L HU. Information on pay grading and the annual salary scale can be found here: https://hu.berlin/ETRL . Information pursuant to Art. 12, 13 DSGVO on the processing of personal data at Humboldt-Universität zu Berlin within the framework of job advertisements can be found on our website: https://hu.berlin/DSGVO . Please visit our website which gives you access to the legally binding German version. Submit application Contact person Prof. Dr.-Ing. habil. Michael Hübner Professor Tel.: +49 30 2093-41252 Email: michael.huebner ☞ Please insert an @ at this point ☜ hu-berlin ☞ Please insert a period at this point de to profile page of Prof. Dr.-Ing. habil. Michael Hübner Department of Computer Science Address Johann-von-Neumann-Haus, Rudower Chaussee 25, 12489 Berlin General contact Tel.: +49 30 2093-41140"
    },
    "https://www.hu-berlin.de/en/university/working-at-the-hu/jobs/details/wissenschaftlicher-mitarbeiterin-m-w-d-auf-dem-gebiet-der-romanischen-sprachen-schwerpunkt-spanisch-dr-164-26": {
      "title": "Research Associate (m/f/d) in the field of Romance Languages (specialising in Spanish)",
      "description": "Research Associate (m/f/d) in the field of Romance Languages (specialising in Spanish) expected full-time position, salary grade E 13 TV-L HU (third-party funded, fixed-term until 31 December 2030) At a glance Job category Research staff and teaching staff Organization Faculty of Language, Literature and Humanities Department of Romance Literatures and Linguistics Location Boeckh-Haus, Dorotheenstraße 65, 10117 Berlin Reference number DR/164/26 Time limitation 31. Dec 2030 Pay grade E13 Job scope Vollzeit (39.4 Hours weekly) Number of vacancies 1 Application deadline 16. Dec 2026 Apply now Your responsibilities Completed university degree and a doctorate in linguistics, computational linguistics, computer science or a related field Excellent command of Spanish, spoken and written (at least C1 level) Excellent command of English, spoken and written (at least C1 level) LLM expertise: sound experience in fine-tuning and instruction tuning (e.g. LoRA), as well as in evaluating LLMs and multilingual transformer models Linguistic annotation: experience with the Universal Dependencies (UD) annotation standards and the CoNLL-U format Knowledge of parsing and parser evaluation (e.g. spaCy) Corpus curation: experience with collaborative annotation tools NLP programming: advanced programming skills in Python with a focus on NLP applications (PyTorch) Experience in GPU computing (CUDA, Google Colab, HPC) Knowledge of statistical analysis methods for evaluating linguistic variation Teaching experience at university level (Bachelor/Master) Demonstrated publication record or demonstrable potential in computational linguistics or NLP Thorough knowledge of word-processing and spreadsheet software Independent, structured and organised way of working, along with the ability to set priorities Strong communication and teamwork skills, plus flexibility in the face of changing project requirements What you bring to the table What we expect from you Completed university degree and a doctorate in linguistics, computational linguistics, computer science or a related field Excellent command of Spanish, spoken and written (at least C1 level) Excellent command of English, spoken and written (at least C1 level) LLM expertise: sound experience in fine-tuning and instruction tuning (e.g. LoRA), as well as in evaluating LLMs and multilingual transformer models Linguistic annotation: experience with the Universal Dependencies (UD) annotation standards and the CoNLL-U format Knowledge of parsing and parser evaluation (e.g. spaCy) Corpus curation: experience with collaborative annotation tools NLP programming: advanced programming skills in Python with a focus on NLP applications (PyTorch) Experience in GPU computing (CUDA, Google Colab, HPC) Knowledge of statistical analysis methods for evaluating linguistic variation Teaching experience at university level (Bachelor/Master) Demonstrated publication record or demonstrable potential in computational linguistics or NLP Thorough knowledge of word-processing and spreadsheet software Independent, structured and organised way of working, along with the ability to set priorities Strong communication and teamwork skills, plus flexibility in the face of changing project requirements What would be desirable Experience with (academic-)administrative involvement (e.g. degree programmes) Demonstrated expertise in (Spanish) dialectology and morphosyntax Knowledge of language technology (ASR) and its integration into annotation pipelines Experience with GIS (geographic information systems) for spatial analysis and visualisation of dialectal distribution Experience with citizen science or crowdsourcing platforms for data collection Previous work on Latin American Spanish varieties Good command of German, spoken and written (at least B1 level) Your path to the HU Please send your complete application, referencing the job ID DR/164/26 , to Humboldt-Universität zu Berlin, Institut für Romanistik, Prof. Dr. Miriam Bouzouita, Unter den Linden 6, 10099 Berlin, or preferably by e-mail as a single PDF file to spanische.linguistik ☞ Please insert an @ at this point ☜ hu-berlin ☞ Please insert a period at this point de . Required application documents: Letter of motivation Curriculum vitae Certificates / degree documents List of publications List of talks, poster presentations and further training Overview of completed and ongoing research projects Evidence of previous teaching experience Research concept for a planned habilitation thesis For questions about the vacancy, Prof. Dr Miriam Bouzouita ( miriam.bouzouita ☞ Please insert an @ at this point ☜ hu-berlin ☞ Please insert a period at this point de ) is happy to assist. The position is scheduled to be filled as of 01. January 2027. T he Humboldt-Universität zu Berlin is seeking to increase the proportion of women in research and teaching, and specifically encourages qualified female scholars to apply. Severely disabled applicants with equivalent qualifications will be given preferential consideration. People with an immigration history are specifically encouraged to apply. Since we will not return your documents, please submit copies in the application only. The Humboldt-Universität zu Berlin is bound by collective agreements and applies the TV-L HU. Information on pay grading and the annual salary scale can be found here: https://hu.berlin/ETRL . Information pursuant to Art. 12, 13 DSGVO on the processing of personal data at Humboldt-Universität zu Berlin within the framework of job advertisements can be found on our website: https://hu.berlin/DSGVO . Please visit our website which gives you access to the legally binding German version. Submit application Contact person Prof. Dr. Miriam Bouzouita Professor Tel.: +49 30 2093-73555 Email: miriam.bouzouita ☞ Please insert an @ at this point ☜ hu-berlin ☞ Please insert a period at this point de Profile page of Prof. Dr. Miriam Bouzouita Department of Romance Literatures and Linguistics Address Boeckh-Haus, Dorotheenstraße 65, 10117 Berlin General contact Tel.: +49 30 2093-73555"
    },
    "https://www.hu-berlin.de/en/university/working-at-the-hu/jobs/details/juniorprofessur-w1-fuer-britische-geschichte-und-die-geschichte-des-britischen-empire-mit-tenure-track-nach-w2-jp-003-26": {
      "title": "Junior Professorship (W1) for “British History and the History of the British Empire” (with tenure track to full professorship W2)",
      "description": "Junior Professorship (W1) for “British History and the History of the British Empire” (with tenure track to full professorship W2) from 1 April 2028 At a glance Job category Professors and assistant professors Organization Humboldt University Centre for British Studies Location Bürogebäude, Schönhauser Allee 10-11, 10119 Berlin Reference number JP/003/26 Pay grade W1 Job scope Vollzeit (40 Hours weekly) Number of vacancies 1 Application deadline 15. Dec 2026 Apply now The Centre for British Studies invites applications for a Junior Professorship (W1) for “British History and the History of the British Empire” (with tenure track to full professorship W2) from 1 April 2028. This position is a tenure-track position (W2). No later than 15 months before the end of the tenure-track professorship, an evaluation procedure is initiated with the aim of determining whether the performance requirements for a lifetime appointment have been met. Tenure-track professors at HU Berlin are expected to perform in the areas of research, academic teaching, participation in academic self-government, support of early-career researchers and the acquisition of personnel management skills. The specific performance requirements are determined in the course of the appointment procedure and are based on the framework catalogue ( https://hu.berlin/TT-Rahmenkatalog ). The Centre for British Studies is an interdisciplinary research and teaching centre at HU Berlin („Zentralinstitut“). What you bring to the table Successful candidates will have a degree in history and a PhD with a historical focus, and a proven track record and interest in other disciplines and methods. An interest in gender history would be welcomed. The postholder is expected to teach on the international, interdisciplinary and English-language only Master in British Studies and at the Institut für Geschichtswissenschaften (HU), to develop interdisciplinary research projects, to take a leading role in the Graduate School for British Studies and the Berlin Britain Research Network, in the Centre’s high-level knowledge transfer activities, as well as seeking third-party funding and developing the Centre’s public profile in general. Successful candidates need to have a working knowledge of German with a view to expanding it to a C1 level, and will be required to take on administrative functions in German. They are expected to be able to speak and write English to near-native level. They should furthermore have an interest in developing teaching formats for heterogeneous groups, have a proven track record of excellent research, publication, and teaching, and experience with knowledge exchange. The successful applicant will be expected to promote the Oxford-Berlin partnership and intensify links between other research departments and faculties within HU and the Berlin University Alliance. More information about the Centre can be found at www.gbz.hu-berlin.de . The applicants must meet the legal requirements for professorial appointments in conjunction with § 102c combined with § 102a of the ‘Berliner Hochschulgesetz’. Your path to the HU HU is seeking to increase the proportion of women in research and teaching, and specifically encourages qualified female scholars to apply. Researchers from abroad are welcome to apply. Severely disabled applicants with equivalent qualifications will be given preferential consideration. People with an immigration history are specifically encouraged to apply. Please send your application until 15 th Dec 2026 , referencing the job ID JP/003/26 to: Humboldt-Universität zu Berlin, Director of the Centre for British Studies, Prof. Dr. Gesa Stedman (located: Schönhauser Allee 10-11, 10119 Berlin), Unter den Linden 6, 10099 Berlin or in electronic form in one pdf file to Verwaltung.gbz _svTElvYxKa @ ☞ Please insert an @ at this point ☜ hu-berlin _I58goCVZX0 . ☞ Please insert a period at this point de . Since we will not return your documents, please submit copies in the application only. Applications should include a covering letter (addressed to Prof. Dr Gesa Stedman), a full CV, a complete list of publications, a list of ongoing and completed research projects including third-party funding track record, an up-to-date record of taught courses including teaching methods, formats, and supervision experience, and a one-page list of projects and ideas on how to take the Centre for British Studies into its next 10 years. Information pursuant to Art. 12, 13 DSGVO on the processing of personal data at Humboldt-Universität zu Berlin within the framework of job advertisements can be found on our website: https://hu.berlin/DSGVO . Please visit our website which gives you access to the legally binding German version. Submit application Centre for British Studies Address Bürogebäude, Schönhauser Allee 10-11, 10119 Berlin General contact Tel.: +49 30 2093-99040 gbz _Y2zLRMe45g @ ☞ Please insert an @ at this point ☜ gbz.hu-berlin _EkKkGc2nmT . ☞ Please insert a period at this point de"
    },
    "https://www.hu-berlin.de/en/university/working-at-the-hu/jobs/details/junior-professorship-w1-with-tenure-track-to-w3-for-history-didactics-jp-004-26": {
      "title": "Junior Professorship (W1 with Tenure Track to W3) for ‘History Didactics’",
      "description": "Junior Professorship (W1 with Tenure Track to W3) for ‘History Didactics’ from 1st October 2027 At a glance Job category Professors and assistant professors Organization Faculty of Arts and Humanities Department of History Location Institutsgebäude, Friedrichstraße 191, 10117 Berlin Reference number JP/004/26 Pay grade W1 Job scope Vollzeit (40 Hours weekly) Number of vacancies 1 Application deadline 17. Dec 2026 Apply now The Faculty of Humanities, Department of History, invites applications for a Junior Professorship (W1 with Tenure Track to W3) for ‘History Didactics’ from 1 st October 2027. Applicants are expected to have a proven record of expertise in history didactics / history education and teacher education, combined with clear links to history as an academic discipline. Experience with, or critical reflection on, cross-disciplinary challenges such as media education, inclusion, democracy education or sustainability, as well as possible connections to the Institute’s research areas, in particular digitality and mediality as well as Europe, are welcome. Since the position carries responsibility for teacher education across all school types, three years of school teaching experience are required. This position is a tenure-track position. No later than 15 months before the end of the tenure-track professorship, an evaluation procedure is initiated with the aim of determining whether the performance requirements for a lifetime appointment have been met. Tenure-track professors at HU Berlin are expected to perform in the areas of research, academic teaching, participation in academic self-government, support of early-career researchers and the acquisition of personnel management skills. The specific performance requirements are determined in the course of the appointment procedure and are based on the framework catalogue ( https://hu.berlin/TT-Rahmenkatalog ). As part of the professorship, the successful candidate will also be expected to contribute to the Professional School of Education (PSE), the Humboldt-Universität zu Berlin's central institute for teacher education. What you bring to the table For this professorship at Humboldt-Universität zu Berlin, we seek an an academically distinguished scholar with an independent research profile and demonstrated familiarity with a broad range of research fields and methodologies in history education and historical learning. In addition to a completed university degree and pedagogical aptitude, applicants must demonstrate a special aptitude for academic work, usually evidenced by the outstanding quality of their doctorate. Applicants are expected to submit reflections on a second research focus; this research focus need not yet have been published, but should be outlined in the concept paper attached to the application. Experience in university teaching is also desirable, as is a commitment to academic self-governance within the university and to self-governance structures in teacher education. The applicants must meet the legal requirements for professorial appointments in conjunction with § 102c combined with § 102a of the ‘Berliner Hochschulgesetz’. With this professorship, Humboldt-Universität zu Berlin aims to address and support scholars at an early career stage. HU is seeking to increase the proportion of women in research and teaching, and specifically encourages qualified female scholars to apply. Researchers from abroad are welcome to apply. Severely disabled applicants with equivalent qualifications will be given preferential consideration. People with an immigration history are specifically encouraged to apply. Your path to the HU Please send your application, referencing the job ID JP/004/26 to: Humboldt-Universität zu Berlin, Dean of the Faculty of Humanities, Unter den Linden 6, 10099 Berlin or preferably by email as a single PDF file to berufungen.philfak ☞ Please insert an @ at this point ☜ hu-berlin ☞ Please insert a period at this point de . Since we will not return your documents, please submit copies in the application only. Applications should include: a cover letter; a curriculum vitae; a list of publications; a detailed report on previous research and teaching activities at schools and universities; a concept paper on the future orientation of the professorship (maximum five pages); a statement (maximum one page) on past and future contributions to equal opportunities, diversity and inclusion, as well as on the ability to work in culturally diverse groups; copies of certificates and diplomas. Information pursuant to Art. 12, 13 DSGVO on the processing of personal data at Humboldt-Universität zu Berlin within the framework of job advertisements can be found on our website: https://hu.berlin/DSGVO . Please visit our website which gives you access to the legally binding German version. Submit application Department of History Address Institutsgebäude, Friedrichstraße 191, 10117 Berlin General contact ifg-sekretariat ☞ Please insert an @ at this point ☜ hu-berlin ☞ Please insert a period at this point de"
    },
    "https://www.hu-berlin.de/en/university/working-at-the-hu/jobs/details/nachwuchsgruppenleiterin-m-w-d-im-exzellenzcluster-math-dr-178-26": {
      "title": "Head of junior research group (m/f/d) in the Cluster of Excellence MATH+ in the field of algebraic geometry and AI",
      "description": "Head of junior research group (m/f/d) in the Cluster of Excellence MATH+ in the field of algebraic geometry and AI expected full-time employment - E 14 TV-L HU (third-party funding limited until 31.12.2032) At a glance Job category Research staff and teaching staff Organization Faculty of Mathematics and Natural Sciences Department of Mathematics Location Johann-von-Neumann-Haus, Rudower Chaussee 25, 12489 Berlin Reference number DR/178/26 Time limitation 31. Dec 2032 Pay grade E14 Job scope Vollzeit (39.4 Hours weekly) Number of vacancies 1 Application deadline 30. Dec 2026 Apply now The junior research group will be based at the Department of Mathematics at Humboldt-Universität zu Berlin and integrated into the local research environment in algebra and algebraic geometry. This includes integration into the Cluster of Excellence MATH+ – Berlin Mathematics Research Center. MATH+ connects mathematical research at Humboldt-Universität, Freie Universität, and Technische Universität Berlin, as well as at the Weierstrass Institute and the Zuse Institute Berlin. The head of the junior research group is expected to contribute to establishing new connections between algebraic geometry/algebra and rapidly developing research areas within the field of Artificial Intelligence for Mathematics. Your responsibilities scientific services in research on interdisciplinary scientific issues in the MATH+ context: application-oriented research that encompasses mathematics as well as disciplines Computer Science and Physics. possible research directions include: the use of machine learning and artificial intelligence methods to investigate algebraic-geometric structures the computer-aided discovery of patterns, structures, and conjectures in algebraic geometry or related fields the integration of symbolic computation, computational algebraic geometry, and modern machine learning methods generative models for mathematical — and specifically algebraic-geometric — structures automated and formalized mathematical reasoning and theorem proving the development of algebraic and geometric methods to gain a mathematical understanding of modern AI systems. This list is not exhaustive. Original research programs that establish new connections between algebraic geometry (algebra) and AI for mathematics are particularly welcome. development of an independent and internationally visible research program, supervision of early-career researchers, and actively participation in the scientific life of the Institute of Mathematics at Humboldt-Universität, as well as MATH+ and the Berlin Mathematical School What you bring to the table completed scientific university education and excellent doctorate in mathematics or related subjects internationally recognized research achievements in algebraic geometry or a closely related field internationally visible research achievements in Algebraic Geometry or a closely related field, as well as experience with (international) research collaborations several years of scientific activity after completing studies, several years of independent research experience in Germany or abroad in the field of Algebraic Geometry or a closely related field compelling scientific concept for linking algebraic geometry with artificial intelligence methods interest in interdisciplinary and cross-institutional collaboration within Humboldt-Universität and MATH+ willingness to participate in the training and supervision of doctoral candidates within the Berlin Mathematical School prior specialization or an extensive publication record in machine learning or artificial intelligence is not required applications are particularly welcome from outstanding early-career researchers in algebraic geometry or related fields who develop a compelling concept for how artificial intelligence methods can open up new mathematical lines of inquiry applications are also welcome from researchers who are already working at the intersection of pure mathematics, computational mathematics, and artificial intelligence, and whose research program has a clear focus on algebraic geometry solid experience in heterogeneous, interdisciplinary groups; knowledge and experience in higher education didactics experience in collaboration with committees and designated officers; very good knowledge of the relevant target groups excellent programming skills, preferably in Python, as well as experience with mathematical software (Sage, Macaulay 2, Singular or Magma) very good knowledge of English (at least C1 level) planning and organizational skills; independent, structured and goal-oriented work; above-average stress tolerance; team spirit and strong communication skills What we offer Special opportunities for collaboration arise from Research Training Group 2965, \"From Geometry to Numbers: Moduli, Hodge Theory, Rational Points\" jointly supported by Humboldt-Universität zu Berlin and Leibniz Universität Hannover. Close ties with the Berlin Mathematical School (BMS) are envisaged. The BMS is the joint graduate school for mathematics in Berlin and the graduate school of MATH+. This will allow the head of the junior research group to recruit doctoral candidates from an international pool of applicants, offer courses and seminars within the BMS program, and participate in structured doctoral training as well as have access to the scientific infrastructure of the Institute of Mathematics, MATH+, and the Berlin Mathematical School, specifically access to the corresponding seminar, guest, and research activities . The Junior Group Leader will be supported in acquiring their own third-party funding and in establishing national and international collaborations. We offer flexible working hours (flexitime) and salary classification under the collective bargaining agreement (TV-L). As a family-friendly university, we promote the compatibility of work and family life. Your path to the HU Please send your complete application, referencing the job ID DR/178/26 to Humboldt-Universität zu Berlin, Faculty of Mathematics and Natural Sciences, Department of Mathematics, Prof. Dr. Gavril Farkas (located: Rudower Chaussee 25, 12489 Berlin-Adlershof), Unter den Linden 6, 10099 Berlin or preferably in electronic form as a single PDF file to gavril.farkas _tLN7e7537C @ ☞ Please insert an @ at this point ☜ hu-berlin _rgmv8q8bbl . ☞ Please insert a period at this point de . Required application documents: scholarly cover letter detailed curriculum vitae list of publications proof of the required qualification (certificates, diplomas, continuing education certificates) selected scholarly works overview of research conducted to date details regarding teaching experience and student supervision contact details for suitable academic referees research proposal on “Algebraic Geometry and Artificial Intelligence” (approximately 3–5 pages), that should explain: Which fundamental questions of algebraic geometry are to be investigated; What role artificial intelligence methods play in this context; What new mathematical methods or structures might emerge from this connection; How the research program fits into the field of algebraic geometry at Humboldt-Universität zu Berlin; and which connections are to be established with MATH+ and the Berlin Mathematical School If you have further questions about the job posting or the scope of duties, please do not hesitate to contact Prof. Dr. Gavril Farkas ( gavril.farkas _XmFzUqYDO3 @ ☞ Please insert an @ at this point ☜ hu-berlin _CLuNUyqpa9 . ☞ Please insert a period at this point de ). The position is scheduled to be filled on the earliest possible date . The Humboldt-Universität zu Berlin is seeking to increase the proportion of women in research and teaching, and specifically encourages qualified female scholars to apply. Severely disabled applicants with equivalent qualifications will be given preferential consideration. People with an immigration history are specifically encouraged to apply. Since we will not return your documents, please submit copies in the application only. The Humboldt-Universität zu Berlin is bound by collective agreements and applies the TV-L HU. Information on pay grading and the annual salary scale can be found here: https://hu.berlin/ETRL . Information pursuant to Art. 12, 13 DSGVO on the processing of personal data at Humboldt-Universität zu Berlin within the framework of job advertisements can be found on our website: https://hu.berlin/DSGVO . Please visit our website which gives you access to the legally binding German version. Submit application Contact person Prof. Dr. Gavril Farkas Professor Tel.: +49 30 2093-45442 Email: farkas _P0k83n9s1u @ ☞ Please insert an @ at this point ☜ math.hu-berlin _YJZVecwAMt . ☞ Please insert a period at this point de Profile page of Prof. Dr. Gavril Farkas Department of Mathematics Address Johann-von-Neumann-Haus, Rudower Chaussee 25, 12489 Berlin General contact Tel.: +49 30 2093-45300 institut-mathematik.sek _fU04JG25Gl @ ☞ Please insert an @ at this point ☜ hu-berlin _VhFaZIsfCM . ☞ Please insert a period at this point de"
    },
    "https://www.hu-berlin.de/en/university/working-at-the-hu/jobs/details/wissenschaftlicher-mitarbeiterin-m-w-d-im-bereich-pflanzenernaehrung-an-245-26": {
      "title": "Research Associate (m/f/d) in Plant Nutrition",
      "description": "Research Associate (m/f/d) in Plant Nutrition fixed-term contract for a maximum of 6 years in accordance with the German Academic Fixed-Term Contract Act (WissZeitVG) – salary grade E 13 TV-L HU At a glance Job category Research staff and teaching staff Organization Faculty of Life Sciences Albrecht Daniel Thaer-Institute of Agricultural and Horticultural Sciences Location Albrecht-Thaer-Weg 4, 14195 Berlin Reference number AN/245/26 Time limitation in months 72 Pay grade E13 Job scope Vollzeit (39.4 Hours weekly) Number of vacancies 1 Application deadline 16. Dec 2026 Apply now Founded in 1810, Humboldt-Universität zu Berlin is one of Germany’s leading universities. As a comprehensive university with more than 36,000 students, it combines research excellence with innovative support for early-career researchers. Its international networks, interdisciplinary research collaborations and progressive teaching concepts help to shape Berlin as a centre of scholarship and science. Humboldt-Universität holds the status of a University of Excellence. Your responsibilities scientific service in research and teaching in the field of plant nutrition acquisition of third-party funding, project management and publication of peer-reviewed scientific papers tasks toward your own further academic qualification (habilitation) What you bring to the table What we expect from you completed scientific university degree (Bachelor’s and Master’s degree) and/or doctorate in agricultural or environmental sciences or a comparable academic discipline i nitial independent and innovative publications in English-language, peer-reviewed academic journals i deally, initial experience in acquiring third-party funding practical research experience with field and greenhouse experiments practical experience in the physical and wet-chemical preparation of soil, fertilizer and plant samples for chemical analysis practical research experience in processing raw data and statistically analysing experimental datasets, such as concentration data and stable-isotope data from plant growth experiments practical experience in supervising students undertaking academic work in plant nutrition or a comparable academic discipline experience in planning and delivering university courses, including lectures, seminars and practical classes very good written and spoken English skills at a minimum level C1 enthusiasm for teamwork, particularly with technical and administrative staff and with students What would be desirable experience with, or willingness to apply and further develop, stable-isotope methods in plant nutrition German language skills at a minimum of CEFR level B2 (for administrative communication) What we offer a modern and inspiring work environment a pay scale classification (TV-L) high responsibility in different working fields structured orientation and onboarding excellent opportunities for further training As a family-friendly university, we support the compatibility of work and family life. Your path to the HU Please send your complete application, referencing the job ID AN/245/26 to Humboldt-Universität zu Berlin, Faculty of Life Sciences, Albrecht Daniel Thaer Institute of Agricultural and Horticultural Sciences, Chair of Plant Nutrition, Prof. Dr. Matthias Wiggenhauser (located: Albrecht-Thaer-Weg 4, 14195 Berlin), Unter den Linden 6, 10099 Berlin, Germany, or preferably in electronic form as a single PDF file to matthias.wiggenhauser _kphealoaqC @ ☞ Please insert an @ at this point ☜ hu-berlin _AdZFhmbjvK . ☞ Please insert a period at this point de . Required application documents: letter of motivation (one/two pages, including a research and teaching vision) tabular curriculum vitae proof of the required qualification (certificates, diplomas, continuing education certificates) work references or evaluations If you have further questions about the job posting or the scope of duties, please do not hesitate to contact Prof. Dr. Wiggenhauser ( matthias.wiggenhauser _dOIr9j3Kwq @ ☞ Please insert an @ at this point ☜ hu-berlin _UuIxXYs4I4 . ☞ Please insert a period at this point de ). The position is scheduled to be filled on March 1, 2027 The Humboldt-Universität zu Berlin is seeking to increase the proportion of women in research and teaching, and specifically encourages qualified female scholars to apply. Severely disabled applicants with equivalent qualifications will be given preferential consideration. People with an immigration history are specifically encouraged to apply. Since we will not return your documents, please submit copies in the application only. The Humboldt-Universität zu Berlin is bound by collective agreements and applies the TV-L HU. Information on pay grading and the annual salary scale can be found here: https://hu.berlin/ETRL . Information pursuant to Art. 12, 13 DSGVO on the processing of personal data at Humboldt-Universität zu Berlin within the framework of job advertisements can be found on our website: https://hu.berlin/DSGVO . Please visit our website which gives you access to the legally binding German version. Submit application Contact person Prof. Dr. Matthias Wiggenhauser Professor Tel.: +49 30 2093-46490 Email: matthias.wiggenhauser _w42VzB1s62 @ ☞ Please insert an @ at this point ☜ hu-berlin _P02IxXowoa . ☞ Please insert a period at this point de Profile page of Prof. Dr. Matthias Wiggenhauser Albrecht Daniel Thaer-Institute of Agricultural and Horticultural Sciences Address Thaer-Gebäude/Hauptgebäude, Invalidenstraße 42, 10115 Berlin General contact Tel.: +49 30 2093-46300 thaerinstitut _FIwsNv5qhR @ ☞ Please insert an @ at this point ☜ hu-berlin _qyBzG9pets . ☞ Please insert a period at this point de"
