      "title": "Research Fellow (m/f/d) in the field of Animal Husbandry and Ethology",
      "description": "Research Fellow (m/f/d) in the field of Animal Husbandry and Ethology expected 2/3-part-time employment - E 13 TV-L HU (third-party funding limited until 30.09.2029) At a glance Job category Research staff and teaching staff Organization Faculty of Life Sciences Albrecht Daniel Thaer-Institute of Agricultural and Horticultural Sciences Location Lentzeallee 75, 14195 Berlin Reference number DR/183/26 Time limitation 30. Sep 2029 Pay grade E13 Job scope Teilzeit (26.26 Hours weekly) Number of vacancies 1 Application deadline 09. Dec 2026 Apply now This offer is made with the reservation that funding will be provided. Founded in 1810, Humboldt-Universität zu Berlin is one of Germany's leading universities. As a comprehensive university with over 36,000 students, it combines research excellence with innovative support for young talents. Their international networks, interdisciplinary research collaborations, and progressive teaching concepts shape Berlin as a center of science. The Humboldt-Universität zu Berlin holds the status of a university of excellence. Your responsibilities scientific service in research in the project: „Ruffled minds? Towards novel technology to assess the welfare of bulls as a neglected animal category” (EUPAHW) planning and coordination of direct and automated recording of behaviour, health and efficiency of finishing bulls execution of behavioural tests with bulls observations and data collection in Scotland application of one of the automated methods on practical farms (D, UK) data processing and analysis using the statistics software R writing of peer-reviewed publications science transfer to the agricultural practice opportunity for personal scientific qualification (doctorate) What you bring to the table What we expect from you completed scientific university degree in agriculture, animal behaviour, veterinary medicine, or in a related field experience with animal behavioural studies comprehensive statistical knowledge experience with automatically collected data knowledge of handling of large data sets profound knowledge of word processing software proficiency in spoken and written German (at least C1) proficiency in spoken and written English (at least C1) very good communication and teamwork skills What would be desirable driving license cat. B experience in handling large animals What we offer collaboration in a multi-national project (A, D, N, UK) and a versatile project team a modern work environment a pay scale classification (TV-L) high responsibility in different working fields opportunities for further training As a family-friendly university, we promote the compatibility of work and family life. Your path to the HU Please send your complete application, referencing the job ID DR/183/26 to Humboldt-Universität zu Berlin , Faculty of Life Sciences, Thaer-Institute of Agricultural and Horticultural Sciences, PD Dr. Lorenz Gygax (located: Lentzeallee 75), Unter den Linden 6, 10099 Berlin or preferably in electronic form as a single PDF file to lorenz.gygax _hubtTlFE1S @ ☞ Please insert an @ at this point ☜ hu-berlin _yYw3UgP7mj . ☞ Please insert a period at this point de . Required application documents: letter of motivation tabular curriculum vitae proof of the required qualification (certificates, diplomas, continuing education certificates) work references or evaluations If you have further questions about the job posting or the scope of duties, please do not hesitate to contact Lorenz Gygax ( lorenz.gygax _x1Ao1gkMN1 @ ☞ Please insert an @ at this point ☜ hu-berlin _rG5KlQVQki . ☞ Please insert a period at this point de ). The position is scheduled to be filled on February, 1 st 2027 . The Humboldt-Universität zu Berlin is seeking to increase the proportion of women in research and teaching, and specifically encourages qualified female scholars to apply. Disabled applicants with equivalent qualifications will be given preferential consideration. People with an immigration history are specifically encouraged to apply. Since we will not return your documents, please only submit copies in the application. The Humboldt-Universität zu Berlin is bound by collective agreements and applies the TV-L HU. Information on pay grading and the annual salary scale can be found here: https://hu.berlin/ETRL . Information pursuant to Art. 12, 13 DSGVO on the processing of personal data at Humboldt-Universität zu Berlin within the framework of job advertisements can be found on our website: https://hu.berlin/DSGVO . Please visit our website which gives you access to the legally binding German version. Submit application Contact person PD Dr. Lorenz Gygax Research Assistant Tel.: +49 30 2093-46932 Email: lorenz.gygax _1PHZHjkNd2 @ ☞ Please insert an @ at this point ☜ hu-berlin _XlCgg4mzGf . ☞ Please insert a period at this point de Profile page of PD Dr. Lorenz Gygax Albrecht Daniel Thaer-Institute of Agricultural and Horticultural Sciences Address Thaer-Gebäude/Hauptgebäude, Invalidenstraße 42, 10115 Berlin General contact Tel.: +49 30 2093-46300 thaerinstitut _jDYAhupuTs @ ☞ Please insert an @ at this point ☜ hu-berlin _E7KRss2mtA . ☞ Please insert a period at this point de"
